<title>BELGIUM: Luxembourg Nov inflation falls to 1.77 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Luxembourg Nov inflation falls to 1.77 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg year-on-year inflation fell to 1.77 percent in November from 1.92 percent in October, Luxembourg's statistics office Statec said on Thursday.</p>
<p>					 Dec 1 *    Nov 1     Dec 1 1995</p>
<p>    Consumer Price Index	 117.28     117.39     n/a</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (pct)	  -0.09	+0.45     n/a</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (pct)	    +1.77	+1.92     n/a</p>
<p>NOTE * Consumer Price Index on Dec 1 equals November inflation</p>
<p>In a statement, Statec said the main reason for the fall in inflation was lower heating oil prices.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
